  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "The current best configuration is RNA-only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool (config_005, acc 0.650). The RNA encoder is the dominant design choice since RNA is clearly the strongest modality (0.650 vs 0.208 for image-only), and all future multimodal experiments will build on the RNA backbone. However, scgpt—a second learned encoder—is completely untested, leaving a major gap in our understanding of the encoder landscape. Config_008 (RNA-only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable comparison against config_005, isolating the encoder effect while holding profile setting, aggregation, and modality fixed. This is the highest-information next experiment: if scgpt outperforms scvi_n200, it redefines the best RNA configuration and all subsequent multimodal experiments; if comparable, it confirms scvi_n200 as the preferred learned encoder; if worse, it rules out scgpt and narrows the search. Under a limited budget, resolving which RNA encoder is superior before further multimodal exploration is more informative than testing fusion variants or image encoders on a potentially suboptimal RNA backbone."
}

